History Tracers — What is it?

History Tracers explores humanities, exact sciences, and biological sciences — connecting them through an interdisciplinary approach. It all starts with observing ourselves: counting with our fingers was our first math lesson.

But because we are different peoples, separated for thousands of years without global contact, we reached different solutions to the same goal. The Japanese built the Soroban. The Chinese designed the Suanpan. The Russians created the Schyoty. Three abacuses, three cultures, one idea.

This did not happen only in Eurasia. In America, indigenous peoples developed the Yupana. In Africa, counting became rhythm and music. The Maya explored mathematics through grids.

History Tracers is an open-source platform where you learn through interactive games and educational content — completely free. No paywalls. Just knowledge, for everyone.

Come play. Come learn. History Tracers — free and open source.
